        "response": "Here are three safe ways to protect your email account from phishing:\n\n1. **Use Strong, Unique Passwords and Enable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA):** This is your primary defense. Use complex passwords and always enable 2FA so that even if a hacker gets your password, they can't log in without your phone.\n2. **Be Skeptical of Sender Information:** Always check the sender's actual email address, not just the display name. Look for subtle misspellings or unusual domains that suggest impersonation.\n3. **Hover Before You Click:** Before clicking any link in an email, hover your mouse over it to see the actual destination URL. If the displayed link doesn't match the context of the email, do not click it.",
